      THE LABEL UNDER THE LAUNCHER ICON.

      Android reads this before any JavaScript exists, so it cannot be derived
      from `PRODUCT.name` in `@cartze/core/brand`. `__tests__/appName.test.ts`
      reads this file and fails naming the exact value to paste when the two
      drift.

      It carries the SUFFIX, because a shopkeeper who installs both apps tells
      them apart in a launcher and nowhere else. It was "CartZePartner" — one
      word, which is what an applicationId looks like, not what a person reads.

      NOT an identifier: `com.cartze.partner` and `cartze.partner.auth` are
      addresses and keep their spelling — see `PRODUCT`.
    -->
    <string name="app_name">True Serve Partner</string>
